{%- comment -%}
  ymws-manage-subscriptions-link.liquid
  Yerba Madre Wholesale ‚Äî tag-gated "Manage My Subscriptions" link

  WHAT IT DOES
    Prints a link to the Recharge customer portal ONLY when the logged-in customer currently has the
    Shopify customer tag `wholesale-approved`. Guests, customers without the tag, and customers carrying only
    the other store tags (wholesale-pending, wholesale-rejected, tier-standard) see nothing.

  WHY IT IS "LIVE"
    Liquid's `customer` object is built by Shopify on every request for a logged-in customer. Nothing here is
    cached or stored. The moment the tag is removed in Shopify admin, the very next page load no longer shows
    the link.

  WHAT IT DOES NOT DO
    It only controls whether this LINK is shown. It does not secure the portal itself (the portal URL stays
    reachable) and it does not touch subscriptions. Renewals and portal edits are protected by the Recharge
    quantity-guard extension and the server-side safety net. It reads tags only; it never writes to the
    customer record, so no tag can be removed or overwritten by it.

  USAGE (anywhere in the theme where `customer` is available)
    {% render 'ymws-manage-subscriptions-link' %}

    Optional overrides:
    {% render 'ymws-manage-subscriptions-link',
         link_text: 'Manage My Subscriptions',
         portal_url: '/tools/recurring/login',
         css_class: 'button button--secondary' %}

  CONFIRM BEFORE GO-LIVE
    `portal_url` defaults to Recharge's standard entry point (/tools/recurring/login), which Recharge redirects to
    the current portal location. Click it as an approved test customer and confirm it lands in the portal.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ymws_approval_tag = 'wholesale-approved'
  assign ymws_link_text = link_text | default: 'Manage My Subscriptions'
  assign ymws_portal_url = portal_url | default: '/tools/recurring/login'
  assign ymws_css_class = css_class | default: 'ymws-manage-subscriptions'

  # Tag match is exact on the tag name, ignoring letter case and stray spaces (Shopify treats tags case-insensitively).
  assign ymws_approved = false
  if customer
    for ymws_tag in customer.tags
      assign ymws_tag_normalized = ymws_tag | strip | downcase
      if ymws_tag_normalized == ymws_approval_tag
        assign ymws_approved = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{%- if ymws_approved -%}
  <a class="{{ ymws_css_class | escape }}" href="{{ ymws_portal_url | escape }}">{{ ymws_link_text | escape }}</a>
{%- endif -%}
